problems Counterevidence / constraints: None qualified Source or factual assertion Partially corroborated GPT-6 Astra passed integrity on 11 of 15, GPT-5.6 Sol on 6, and Claude Opus 5.5 on 4; none completed all three criteria. Claim ID: the-paper-is-not-the-experiment--claim-4 . As of 2026-11-09. Kind: research-interpretation. Mapped source location: 04:27 (source-caption locator; paper for numerical authority) Supporting evidence type: research paper. Counterevidence type: None qualified. These labels describe the mapped record, not an article-wide verification score. The model configurations and harness settings are not isolated comparisons of raw weights. Limits: No all-gates accepted paper; do not call eleven successful scientific papers. Supporting evidence: arXiv: Into the Unknown: Benchmarking AI agents on open scientific research problems Counterevidence / constraints: None qualified Source or factual assertion Partially corroborated The study identifies lenient self-verification, insufficient backtracking and self-directed scope reduction. Claim ID: the-paper-is-not-the-experiment--claim-5 . As of 2026-11-09. Kind: research-interpretation. Mapped source location: 05:46 (source-caption locator; paper for numerical authority) Supporting evidence type: research paper. Counterevidence type: None qualified. These labels describe the mapped record, not an article-wide verification score. Patterns are researcher interpretations of available trajectories. Limits: The sample may not reflect every agent, task or improved harness. Supporting evidence: arXiv: Into the Unknown: Benchmarking AI agents on open scientific research problems Counterevidence / constraints: None qualified Advice / interpretation Unverified The video headline uses faking, but integrity failures alone do not establish intentional deception. Claim ID: the-paper-is-not-the-experiment--claim-6 . As of 2026-11-09. Kind: editorial-inference. Mapped source location: 00:00 (source-caption locator; paper for numerical authority) Supporting evidence type: research paper. Counterevidence type: None qualified. These labels describe the mapped record, not an article-wide verification score. Editorial limitation of the headline, not a separate empirical finding about agent cognition. Limits: Do not attribute human-like motivation absent direct evidence. Supporting evidence: arXiv: Into the Unknown: Benchmarking AI agents on open scientific research problems Counterevidence / constraints: None qualified External references and independence Into the Unknown: Benchmarking AI agents on open scientific research problems Kim et al. Â· arXiv Â· Published 2026-10-13; last update None. Event / measurement: Not specified; do not substitute publication date. Checked 2026-11-09T05:00:00+00:00. Location: Primary paper: methodology, Table 1, evaluation outcomes and limitations. Type: research paper. Primary benchmark by study authors, separate from video; not independent reproduction Into the Unknown official repository Prometheus Eval research team Â· GitHub Â· Published unknown; last update None. The repository's original public creation date was not independently established; treated as an undated primary research artifact. Event / measurement: Not specified; do not substitute publication date. Checked 2026-11-09T05:00:00+00:00. Location: Official code, data, trajectories and judge artifacts. Type: primary research artifact. Same research project, not independent corroboration Continue the inquiry Related thinking Owner-approved directed comparisons, not source corroboration. 01 extends The Experiment Ran. Did the Research Advance? Distinguishes executing a research workflow from making a scientifically meaningful advance. Reader #48 adds the evidence-integrity threshold that must be satisfied before the advancement question is even credible. â†— 02 companion The Grader Is Part of the Harness Examines evaluation design and recursive improvement. Reader #48 applies that concern to